usb: phy: add the Unisoc UMS9632 USB 2.0 PHY, peripheral mode

"sprd,ums9632-phy" as a legacy usb_phy with an otg, which is what the MUSB glue (patches/0006) looks for behind
its "usb-phy" phandle. Decoded from the vendor's 6.6 module usb-phy-sprd-hs.ko (its UMS9632 tables and v4 ops):
init turns on otg_ref_eb, powers the PHY up (AON_APB 0x350 PD_L/PD_S, analog 0x18 and AON_APB 0x190 isolation),
selects the 16-bit UTMI, pulses phy_rst/utmi_rst, sets device mode with the trim (analog 0x10) and reports VBUS
valid (AON_APB 0x204 bit 24, analog 0x04 bit 16), as the vendor does on a cable connect: there is no charger or
extcon driver yet. Needs the two syscons (MFD_SYSCON). The efuse trim is applied when an nvmem provider for it
exists, which mainline does not have for this SoC yet.

The glue now looks the PHY up before its resets and leaves the two reset lines, which are the PHY's too, to the
PHY driver when there is one.

